1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,040
Hey, Rifleheads!

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:06,360
What's a guy gotta do to
get a little food in here?

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:07,630
Kars!

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,894
This man's mechanical!

5
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:15,180
You're von Stroheim!

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:16,560
Double shock!

7
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:22,395
This is spookier than meeting a ghost
in a dark cemetery after midnight!

8
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:24,810
Kars!

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,577
And von Stroheim,

10
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:30,517
who I could have sworn was blown
into little tiny bits back in Mexico!

11
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:33,129
They're both standing
right in front of me!

12
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:45,360
Shijima-no-soko-kara

13
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:50,220
Meta-menu-sono-hasira-tachi

14
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,000
Thank you.

15
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,720
Nihilishimete

16
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,520
von Stroheim.

17
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:26,040
George, as you can see,
I'm back from hell.

18
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,540
Should I be happy about

19
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:31,290
it?

20
00:02:31,373 --> 00:02:33,800
When you get down to it,
he's not exactly a bad guy,

21
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:36,337
except for the fact that
he's a damn German soldier,

22
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:39,937
and I don't like the way he struts around
like he's better than everyone else.

23
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,360
Still, I am a bit

24
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:42,850
happy.

25
00:02:42,933 --> 00:02:47,066
Why don't you make yourself at home on
the sofa and watch me while I do my work?

26
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:52,650
He...

27
00:02:52,733 --> 00:02:53,700
he's glaring at me.

28
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:58,740
He knows that I'm the one who
killed ACDC, and he hates me for it.

29
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:01,920
Even so... Kars!

30
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:06,216
Do you think I'm gonna just sit here
and let you try and fight me out?!

31
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:13,580
Jojo, once I'm finished securing the
stone, I'm going to put an end to you.

32
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:17,297
It's too bad Wamuu is still
off working in Greece.

33
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:22,260
I can't allow a Hamon user who was
able to beat AC-DC to remain alive.

34
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,697
Tell me something, Kars.

35
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:24,917
Do you speak as a warrior?

36
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,706
Or are you after something
else, like revenge?

37
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:29,860
Pay attention.

38
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,158
You're fighting me.

39
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:34,277
I'm the one who is going
to be your final opponent.

40
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,280
No machine can stop me.

41
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,620
Is that right?

42
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:45,468
Arms of flesh and blood can't bend like
that, which means they are mechanical.

43
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:48,440
Now for the fun!

44
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,117
Wait, he's...

45
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:54,900
His fingers squeeze at 1,950
kilograms per centimeter square!

46
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,219
Almost twice San Viento's strength!

47
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,040
You utter fool!

48
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:02,451
German science is the finest in the world!

49
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:04,940
These arms have such great power!

50
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,911
They were constructed based on
the abilities of San Viento!

51
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:11,170
Unsocar!

52
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:16,197
We've calculated exactly what
we need to do to you in order

53
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:19,633
to eliminate your power and
leave you in desperate agony.

54
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:23,037
I'm going to pluck you like a chicken,

55
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:26,857
beat by beat, and take you apart
one square centimeter at a time.

56
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:31,160
Hey, Jojo, don't you dare even
think about feeling sorry for me.

57
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:36,537
My proud new form is the
very embodiment of the

58
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:39,197
ultimate peak of German
science and engineering.

59
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:42,680
You see, I'm not merely human, I'm more!

60
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,560
Take this, cars.

61
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:47,857
My machine gun can fire
600 rounds per minute and

62
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:51,057
shred through armor plating
like it was made of paper.

63
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:54,660
I'll whittle you down into
tiny pieces in no time at all.

64
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,060
His body's mechanical too?

65
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:14,253
What the hell was that?

66
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:15,792
It came from downstairs.

67
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:19,740
I swear the stone will be mine today.

68
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:22,600
Attempting to get it cost ACDC his life.

69
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:26,467
I refuse to allow his ultimate
sacrifice to have been in vain.

70
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:32,340
That light, the blade coming
out of his arm is glowing.

71
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:34,460
I can control light.

72
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:37,020
Behold, brilliant bone blade.

73
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:43,290
Impossible!

74
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:47,740
That blade is hardened bone and
skin, not weapons-grade forged steel.

75
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:50,837
It shouldn't be able to
deflect bullets like that,

76
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:53,273
let alone slice them in half in mid-air.

77
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:56,820
His blade is amazing, but
why is it glowing like that?

78
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:00,797
I... I...

79
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,100
I know that sound.

80
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:07,387
Upon seeing the blade up close, Von
Stroheim was able to understand its secret.

81
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:09,680
It didn't have a simple edge.

82
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:13,280
Rather, it had a rotating
blade moving at high speed.

83
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:17,597
Tiny, razor-sharp claws slid quietly
along the outer edge of the blade,

84
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,717
ready to shred anything in its path.

85
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:22,137
Each claw was flawlessly
polished to a mirror

86
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:24,697
-like finish and refracted
the faintest light,

87
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:28,309
making the blade look as though
it were glowing from within.

88
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,160
We can't win this!

89
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:36,557
At least not with my weapons or any
modern technology that I know of.

90
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,300
We've got to feed him!

91
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,620
And what was San Bind?

92
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,460
Nothing but a weak child,
a well-trained guard dog.

93
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:47,680
He couldn't even compare to us.

94
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:50,760
Now, I'll take that stone.

95
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:52,740
Kars, what the hell?

96
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:58,120
That ice-cold sheen across his face.

97
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,860
A blade that can cut bullets in midair.

98
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:05,217
There's no way I could ever block
that thing with only my bare hands.

99
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:08,497
Even if I could concentrate all
of my Harmon into a single blow,

100
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:11,286
that blade would still
slice right through me.

101
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:15,898
To be perfectly honest, I
want to run away from here.

102
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,737
He's way too dangerous
to take on directly.

103
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:21,937
I can't think of any way to
get around that blade of his.

104
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:25,432
Then again, I can't just leave
and let him take the stone.

105
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:30,077
If he obtains the stone's power,
he'd become practically invincible.

106
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,042
I'd never be able to defeat him.

107
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,390
Damn it all!

108
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,897
I have to get my hands on Womu's antidote.

109
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:37,862
Kars wants to kill me after all.

110
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:38,810
Why me?

111
00:07:38,893 --> 00:07:40,211
Was this in my horoscope?

112
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,280
What is this?

113
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,168
What's in this pocket here?

114
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:48,200
The Red Stone of Asia.

115
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:51,520
I have waited a long time for this.

116
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,280
5,000 years.

117
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,560
And at last, the stone is mine.

118
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,937
Not that I ever doubted it would be.

119
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:01,180
It was destined to fall
into my hands. Kars!

120
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,057
Just be patient.

121
00:08:05,140 --> 00:08:06,669
I'll kill you in a moment.

122
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,580
Damn, that bastard!

123
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:11,060
He really hates everything about me!

124
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,579
Letting him walk away with the stone
would mean the end for everyone!

125
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:17,940
Kars, you fool!

126
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:22,181
Don't think you've beaten me because
I'm not finished with you yet!

127
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,480
German science is the world's greatest!

128
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,777
I will beat you!

129
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:32,400
Von Stroheim, you idiot!

130
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:33,817
What do you think you're doing?

131
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:36,959
How can you sit there and
boast at a time like this?

132
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:40,307
Ultraviolet beams, activate!

133
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,140
It's the stone!

134
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:49,750
Oh, no!

135
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:52,178
The stone is sliding down the slope!

136
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:56,880
Ah, damn it, no!

137
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:58,337
We have to stop it!

138
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:00,637
The stone is sliding towards the cliff.

139
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,191
If it falls off, it could be lost forever.

140
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,660
What the hell? Look at this.

141
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,852
What's happened in here?

142
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,040
Cars happened.

143
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,976
Jojo, you have to go after the stone.

144
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,827
Grab it while you still can.

145
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:21,120
Damn, he's catching up. He's fast.

146
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,297
He's focused on the stone like a laser.

147
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:24,857
The way he keeps accelerating,

148
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:27,377
he must be planning to grab the
stone and fall off the cliff.

149
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:30,519
He won't be able to stop
before he reaches the edge.

150
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,570
Damn it!

151
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:34,597
The drop beyond that cliff is
at least several hundred meters.

152
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:37,937
With all his superior abilities,
Kars could survive the fall.

153
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:41,737
But it's as high as jumping off the
tallest skyscraper without a parachute.

154
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,526
It'd be certain death for me!

155
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,260
He's passing me!

156
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:52,477
Jojo plans to slow down before he reaches
the edge so he doesn't go flying off,

157
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:53,660
but not Kars!

158
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:54,817
Jojo can't win!

159
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:58,377
There's no way I'm gonna let this
slime get his hands on the stone!

160
00:09:58,460 --> 00:09:59,290
Go!

161
00:09:59,373 --> 00:10:00,203
Run hard, Jojo!

162
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:05,037
Jojo, when I reach down to grab
the stone, I'll be off balance.

163
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,217
With my flank open, I'll be vulnerable.

164
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:08,577
Is that when you'll do it?

165
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,277
Is that when you'll try to kick me?

166
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,190
Huh?

167
00:10:11,273 --> 00:10:12,577
You'll attack me with your hamon,

168
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:15,778
even if it means the stone
disappears into the abyss.

169
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,978
You think your plan will work, Jojo?

170
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:23,880
Oh! Look there! Jojo!

171
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:25,925
You're right on the nose, Kaz!

172
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:27,580
Here it comes!

173
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,540
It's the kick you ordered! No!

174
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,210
Ah!

175
00:10:32,293 --> 00:10:35,557
He's used his legs to pick up the
stone right as Jojo kicked him!

176
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:37,177
He's going to get away with it!

177
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:38,378
I don't believe it!

178
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:41,857
Now, Kaz, what's with that
ridiculously arrogant grin?

179
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,157
I mean, I'm the one who
should be smiling here.

180
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:46,517
I guess I should have
expected as much from you.

181
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:49,820
A trick like that really
isn't good enough to fool me.

182
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:53,717
My kick wasn't aimed at your
vulnerable flank, but rather the snow.

183
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,741
And it worked, just like a break.

184
00:10:58,840 --> 00:10:59,840
What do you know?

185
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:03,077
Looks like I'm the one who
made the nice catch, not you.

186
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,700
Enjoy your trick, cars.

187
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,340
Oh, man, no way!

188
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,820
A blade from his foot!

189
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:11,210
JoJo!

190
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:18,800
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa! Jojo!

191
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:22,220
He's falling viscaz! What's happening?

192
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:25,117
Kaz's blade is starting to
melt itself with my body!

193
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,000
It won't come out! Yaaaah!

194
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:29,840
Y-you son of a bitch!

195
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:32,780
It's 175 meters to the bottom!

196
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,520
Five seconds until impact! Damn!

197
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,797
Falling to my death with this guy?

198
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:38,710
Aaaaah!

199
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:40,260
No thank you!

200
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,182
Swinging Hamon!

201
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,517
He's so heavy!

202
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:50,820
Hamon goes through fluids easily, but ice
and snow are solid and impede the Hamon.

203
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,897
But water is trickling down the ice,

204
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:55,677
so the Hamon can use that
to flow around the solids.

205
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,466
Thus, it's working perfectly!

206
00:11:57,740 --> 00:12:00,622
I don't care what you do,
the stone will be mine!

207
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:02,180
That's it exactly!

208
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:06,000
That tenacity of yours, it's
what scares me the most!

209
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:09,157
I'm best at exploiting
my opponent's negligence,

210
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:12,534
so a tenacious foe is the
absolute worst for me to face!

211
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,897
Tenacity is the opposite of negligence!

212
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:16,720
It will be mine today!

213
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:23,000
More icicles up ahead!

214
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:27,478
Before I can do anything, I have to
get this blade out of my shoulder!

215
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:28,710
Wait!

216
00:12:28,793 --> 00:12:33,040
I can just send Hamon through the blade
and directly into cars! Take this!

217
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:34,260
As I thought,

218
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:37,800
I knew you would try
using my blade against me.

219
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:39,120
Just for that,

220
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,840
it's into the cliff wall with you!

221
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:49,177
and now no wait he's gonna use that
blade and cut me into pieces cars

222
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:53,057
is waiting for jojo to rebound
before he starts cutting him there's

223
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:56,717
no way he can dodge that now i'm
going to take great pleasure in

224
00:12:56,800 --> 00:13:00,976
slicing you in half and picking up
the stone at the bottom of the abyss

225
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:10,657
now you're not about to cut
this are you you wouldn't dare

226
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:13,437
take the chance of chopping the
stone in half along with me.

227
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,977
I can use your own strength
against you by letting

228
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:18,537
your tenacity act as a
defensive measure for me.

229
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:20,780
Now eat this, Kars! I'm on kick!

230
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:28,390
Damn.

231
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:31,257
He's trying to use the
fallen icicles as a rope.

232
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:34,080
He's clever, but they're
in a freefall too.

233
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,060
He'll never reach the top.

234
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:40,620
In that case, allow me to
lend a hand. Hold on. Huh?

235
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:45,730
Caesar!

236
00:13:45,813 --> 00:13:48,113
Hey, nice timing, don't you think, Jojo?

237
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,800
What the hell's going on?

238
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:52,411
And what are you two, some kind of a team?

239
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:56,098
Fusing falling icicle together
to make a rescue rope?

240
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:58,145
I had nothing to do with that.

241
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:01,478
Only Jojo would try something
that colossally stupid.

242
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:02,838
It was predictable.

243
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:06,097
At least you were able
to think up a stupid

244
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,137
trick and then pull it
off in the nick of time.

245
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:09,691
I'm proud of you, Caesar.

246
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:11,060
What was that?

247
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,760
Nice, nice.

248
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:15,480
Real outstanding work, Caesarino.

249
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:19,216
And hey, if Lisa Lisa is up
there, give her a message.

250
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:21,536
I've got the red stone and it's safe.

251
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,426
I kept him from snatching it.

252
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,160
That was a close call.

253
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:28,461
All right, Caesar, you had
better pull him up now.

254
